# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.cursor/mcp.json

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/

# Satellites colocated state (V5 .satellites/ pattern — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
# .satellites/ is mostly operational: the CLI binary, satellites.toml, logs,
# and the worktree — none of which are committed. The committed exceptions are
# the reviewable source trees below. Use `.satellites/*` (glob) not
# `.satellites/` (directory) so those carve-outs take effect.
.satellites/*
# Repo-local substrate sources (sty_afc0769c): project-scoped documents,
# skills, and principles, pushed via `satellites {document,skill,principle}
# upload`. Flat layout .satellites/<kind>/<name>.md; project_id comes from
# satellites.toml. The substrate is the store, these files are the source.
!.satellites/documents/
!.satellites/skills/
!.satellites/principles/
# Workspace/project seeds remain a committed source pushed via
# `satellites seed push`. Each *.md declares its identity; the substrate is
# the store, these files are the reviewable source (not a pull-mirror).
!.satellites/seeds/

# Operator-supplied config — may contain OAuth client secrets. The
# `*.example` templates stay in git; the live files do not.
/scripts/satellites-server.toml
/satellites.toml

# Operator-local backup of .claude/skills (created during a manual move). Never committed.
.claude_bak/
